Package: obs-browser-hid
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: browser source input bridge for OBS Studio
 Adds obs-websocket vendor requests and an in-OBS dock that send
 synthetic keyboard, text and mouse input to named browser sources.
 .
 Quick actions are configurable in the dock, can be bound to OBS
 frontend hotkeys, imported/exported, and can capture click positions
 from the source's interact window.
 .
 The module is installed in the OBS 33+ third-party plugin location
 (/usr/lib/<multiarch>/obs-modules/plugins).

Package: ws-obs
Architecture: any
Section: utils
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: obs-browser-hid
Description: command-line client for OBS obs-websocket vendor requests
 A small WebSocket client for OBS obs-websocket v5. It supports the
 obs-browser-hid vendor (keys, text, mouse clicks and the virtual
 sources "current" and "interact") as well as generic
 CallVendorRequest calls.
